            <div xml:id="d718">

                <pb facs="0857" n="847" sameAs="frus:frus1944v02/pg847"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">840.70/11–144: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Chargé in the
                        Soviet Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Kennan</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-11-01T20:00:00-04:00">November 1, 1944—8
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2581. We have received a note dated October 28 from the Soviet Ambassador here
                    stating that the Polish Committee of National Liberation has requested that it
                    be invited “instead of the Polish <hi rendition="#italic">émigré</hi>
                    Government” to participate in the Conference on Inland Transport being held in
                    London on the grounds that the London Government does not represent Poland. The
                    note continues that the Soviet Government finds this request of the Polish
                    Committee justified and declares that the Soviet Government will not find it
                    possible to continue its participation in this Conference without the
                    participation of the Polish Committee.</p>
                <p>The foregoing is for your information since the Department does not intend to
                    reply immediately to the Soviet note and has, on other <pb facs="0858" n="848"
                        xml:id="pg848"/> grounds, suggested that the Inland Transport Conference in
                    London be recessed for a short interval pending further instructions from the
                    Department. You should not therefore take up or discuss with Soviet officials
                    the question raised in the Soviet note under reference.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stettinius</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
